  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Update of  the San Remo Manual for international humanitarian law at sea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will update the San Remo Manual (1994), a key reference work for international humanitarian law at sea. The aim is to strengthen the protection of civilians and combatants during armed conflict at sea and ensure that the legal framework reflects current technological and operational realities.
Impact: Increased protection of civilians and combatants at sea and stronger adherence to international law applicable to armed conflict at sea.
Outcome: A high quality process involving a large number of states with broad geographical representation, helping to influence state practice in the maritime domain.
The initiative will be carried out through mapping of state practice, consultations, and dialogue with states and experts in several regions, both individually and in groups, and will conclude with a global meeting where the updated manual will be presented.</narrative>
  </description>
